  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Soviet-pattern territorial and mechanised defence tightly integrated with Russia's Union State forces (joint Zapad exercises, Russian Iskander and Oreshnik systems hosted). Large BMP-2/T-72 holdings, new Russian BTR-82A and domestic Volat/Cayman light vehicles, Polonez guided rockets. Has learned drone lessons: quadcopters in almost every company and a domestic counter-UAS system (2026). No combat experience; in game an escalation enemy on the Suwalki Gap and Polish/Lithuanian border.",
    "squad_size": 8,
    "fireteam": "Soviet-pattern 8-9 man motor-rifle squad mounted in BMP-2/BTR. Game: 8 men in 4 pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Defend from prepared positions with mines and anti-tank teams",
      "Mounted counter-attacks with BMP-2 and T-72 supported by artillery",
      "Border provocation and reconnaissance-in-force",
      "Company quadcopters spot for mortars",
      "Smoke and frag use per drill; less initiative than Russian assault troops"
    ],
